    "sbar": {
      "situation": "The bank has recovered from two separate faults, one on payments and one on clearing. Two recovery checks in a row, the last at 21 s, ran the main journey cleanly.",
      "background": "About 12 s before the incident, a pipeline config change on payments set max_transfer_minor from 1000000 to 1. A second later, the clearing worker crashed on queue item 85 with 'JSONDecodeError: Expecting property name enclosed in double quotes' in parse(item).",
      "assessment": "The payments limit change caused nearly every payment to be refused with 422; the incident commander reverted max_transfer_minor to 1000000, which worked. Malformed item 85 crashed clearing and its backlog grew; the incident commander quarantined item 85 and restarted clearing, which brought it back up.",
      "recommendation": "Find out why the pipeline set max_transfer_minor to 1 and stop it recurring. The operations team has been asked (soon) to review clearing item 85: repair and resubmit it, or close it with its customer. Operations should also review the payments wrongly refused with 422 while the limit was 1."
    },
